WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.267
-Our next guest
is a five-time Grammy winner

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.100
and Rock and Roll Hall of Famer

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.701
who has sold
over 185 million records.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.734
Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:14.033
Her fantastic new documentary,
"Janet Jackson,"

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:16.167
just premiered
to record ratings,

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.667
and you can see
all four hours of it

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:20.067
this Friday at 8:00 p.m.
on Lifetime.

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:23.601
Here is the one,
the only Janet Jackson!

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:25.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:29.667
Hi!
Yeah! We love you!

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:32.767
Janet, welcome back!

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.834
I love you, bud.
Congrats on the documentary.

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:38.734
"Janet Jackson"
premiered last week.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.267
Huge hit.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:44.100
Over 15 million people
watched this and loved it.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.467
How does it feel to have it
finally come out?

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.767
-My gosh, it --
it feels great.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:50.968
And I'm so happy.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:53.868
I'm very thankful
that so many people

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:55.434
watched it and enjoyed it.

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:56.767
-I mean, beyond, beyond, beyond.

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:59.234
It was trending number one
on all the socials.

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:02.501
And I'm like, "Oh,
I cannot wait to watch this."

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:06.133
And then, at the same time,
all of your albums

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:08.033
started going back
on the charts.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:12.734
How crazy is that?

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:15.133
I love that that happened!

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:16.767
I love that that happened.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:19.367
Yeah, it was all
such a surprise to me.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:22.100
I was not expecting any of it.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.501
And with the documentary,

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.567
I was just hoping
everyone would enjoy it.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:28.334
-What made you want
to do a documentary?

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:30.934
-Well, you know, I've --
I've had a career.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:32.200
I started when I was 7.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.601
It's been almost 50 years
that I've been doing this.

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:38.467
-That's wild.
-And I thought it would be best

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:41.100
to tell my story, if I can,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.634
as opposed to having
someone else tell it for me.

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:45.501
-Yeah.
I mean, that's wild.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:50.067
'Cause it feels like --
It's fantastic.

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:52.467
But it does -- in a weird way,
it feels like we've known you.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:56.100
Because I knew you as Penny
on "Good Times,"

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.133
and you go like,
"Oh, yeah, we know Janet."

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:00.701
And then Janet Jackson,
you became Janet Jackson.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.334
And "Rhythm Nation"
and everything.

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:04.567
But then you go, "Oh, wait.
We don't really

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:07.000
know you, know you,"
and know what goes on

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.901
in your life and what you were
thinking at the time

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:11.000
or what you were feeling.
And it's like --

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.701
To watch this documentary,
it's like, "Oh, my goodness."

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:15.934
This is --
The amount of just pressure

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:19.434
and everything that goes into
every single aspect of your life

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:22.868
and career and relationships.
It's --

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:25.934
Is it therapeutic
to get it out there?

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:28.234
-It -- ooh!

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:30.634
It was --
It was definitely therapeutic.

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:34.601
It was difficult, at times,
to talk about.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.801
But it --
it definitely was therapeutic.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:40.100
And it took five years to --
to make.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.100
-Wow.
-And I was just really so --

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.968
so worried that people
would find it boring,

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:47.534
to be quite honest with you.

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:50.400
My favorite episode
is the first --

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.567
the very first episode,
because it talks about

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:59.968
my brothers and going back to
that time period and my family.

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:02.000
And that's the episode I enjoy.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.934
And then everything else
related to myself, I was like,

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:07.334
"Oh, my gosh, they're gonna
think this is so boring."

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:10.567
I'm just happy everyone
enjoyed it and got to see it.

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:12.767
-Was it difficult
to pick different memories

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:14.501
and moments
and finding old footage,

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:15.601
never-before-seen footage,

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.300
And you're like,
"Should I release that?

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.968
Should I not?"
I mean, you went for it.

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:22.434
-It was difficult
'cause there was so much --

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.701
so much to pick from.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:28.133
I mean, every tour,
even when I was a kid,

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:29.901
documenting everything.

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:33.868
So it was -- it's hard to tell
your story in four hours.

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:36.300
It's a very difficult
thing to do.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.067
-Yeah. You did it.
-But we managed

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:40.868
to get a good amount in.

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:43.767
-Then you got to go back to your
hometown, to Gary, Indiana,

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:46.234
which you haven't been --
You guys have to see this.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:48.801
It's amazing.
I mean, did you get chills?

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:51.367
Was it weird?
What was it like?

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:52.634
-I -- I loved it.

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:54.667
I hadn't been there
since I was 8.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:58.667
And just everyone in the
neighborhood, they welcomed us.

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:02.234
I went to my brothers'
and sisters' high school

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:06.567
and spent time with the kids
at the school for a minute.

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:08.067
-They must have been thrilled.
-It was just such

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:11.767
a wonderful feeling.
And to know that we all

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:16.267
shared that house
and how small it was.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:17.901
-Yeah, when you're a kid,
it seems giant.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:19.601
-Just incredible for me.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:24.033
There's so many things I learned
about you in this documentary,

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.934
but one is that
you were going to go to --

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:28.334
you wanted to go
to Pepperdine University

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:31.033
and study business law.
-Yeah.

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:32.133
-And then your dad's like,

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:34.534
"No, you're going into
show business."

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:38.200
What dad says, "No,
you're not going to college"?

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.501
You say that in the documentary.
Like, "Who says that?"

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:43.868
-Yeah. Well, you know, everyone
being in show business,

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:47.567
it wouldn't be so bad to be an
entertainment attorney, I guess.

00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:49.634
-Yeah, you're right.
-Still keeping it

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:51.334
within the family.
-Yeah.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:56.100
Quest is actually in -- in the
documentary, as well, talking.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.567
How important was it for you
to put him in?

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.334
And did he pressure you?

00:05:00.334 --> 00:05:03.167
-Hey!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:05.901
-No!
No pressure at all.

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:11.968
It was very important for me to
have Quest in the documentary.

00:05:11.968 --> 00:05:16.300
He played a big part in such
a huge moment in my life.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:19.534
He was a huge supporter
in getting me inducted

00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:21.133
into the
Rock and Roll Hall of Fame,

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:23.834
along with all the fans.

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:26.167
And I just
can't thank him enough.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:29.434
I mean, that's a huge moment
in my career, in my life.

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:31.234
-He loves you so much,
as we all do.

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:33.567
But he really, really,
really loves you, yeah.

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:36.100
Yeah, he's a fan.
He loves you.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.567
[ Applause ]

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:41.734
At the end of the documentary,

00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:47.334
there's a snippet of some
new music called "Love I Love."

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:49.834
And my question is --
I know, I know, I know.

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:51.267
You're like, "Why?
Don't ask me this."

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:54.567
But are we going to get to hear
the song, the whole thing?

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:57.033
And is this hinting
at something?

00:05:57.033 --> 00:05:58.601
What's next?
Tell me something.

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:01.801
-It's so funny because that's --
that's --

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:05.667
It was a song that I recorded
like three years ago.

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:07.334
And in the documentary,
we thought,

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:09.834
"Oh, this would be cool
to put this song right here

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:14.100
at this moment,
this piece in the documentary."

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.400
And everyone
started reacting to it.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:20.734
So, I don't know.
We'll just have to see.

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:24.033
Maybe it'll be a --
You know, we'll see.

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:28.000
-Is there other unreleased
Janet stuff that we --

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.267
like "Love I Love"
that we might see?

00:06:30.267 --> 00:06:32.200
Oh, I know -- don't ask.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:36.968
-I've recorded so many songs
that I've never released.

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:38.868
So, we'll see.
-Wow.

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:40.767
Okay, we'll see.
[ Applause ]

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.234
I want to thank you
for doing our show.

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:43.534
You know we love you.

00:06:43.534 --> 00:06:45.534
Whenever you're in town,
we want to see you.

00:06:45.534 --> 00:06:47.334
And I want to give you
a big hug.

00:06:47.334 --> 00:06:49.968
Congrats on this documentary
and on everything.

00:06:49.968 --> 00:06:52.701
We're the biggest fans of you
over here, so thank you.

00:06:52.701 --> 00:06:54.167
-Thank you so much
for having me.

00:06:54.167 --> 00:06:56.200
It's always a pleasure
being with you guys.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.701
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:57.701 --> 00:06:59.868
Here's Janet Jackson
in her documentary,

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:02.100
"Janet Jackson."
Take a look.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.334
♪ People of the world today ♪

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:06.300
♪ Are we looking
for a better way of life ♪

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:11.033
♪ We are a part
of the Rhythm Nation ♪

00:07:11.033 --> 00:07:13.400
-And it was a big night
for Janet Jackson last night.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.300
She picked up her first-ever
Grammy and became

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.934
the first woman nominated
for Producer of the Year.

00:07:17.934 --> 00:07:19.434
♪♪

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:20.634
-You didn't feel like,
"Oh, my God.

00:07:20.634 --> 00:07:23.133
Like, she's preaching to us."
It was dope.

00:07:23.133 --> 00:07:24.334
-Yeah, it was.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:24.334 --> 00:07:25.968
Janet Jackson, everybody!

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:28.467
You can see all four hours
of the documentary,

00:07:28.467 --> 00:07:31.000
"Janet Jackson,"
this Friday at 8:00 p.m.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.634
on Lifetime
or online at mylifetime.com.

